course: dictionary
lesson: 6912
title: Oyster: more than seafood
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An oyster is a sea animal. Its soft body sits inside a rough, hinged shell that opens and shuts like a little box. Some oysters are eaten as food, but that is only one meaning of the word.
explain: Context tells you which meaning you need. «Backyard hens are given crushed oyster shell» is about the hard shell, not an animal you would eat. Ask yourself: is this sentence about the animal, the shell, or a pearl?
explain: Sometimes the word is part of a saying. «The world is your oyster» does not mean you go out and find oysters. It means you can go anywhere and do anything you choose, which is why it is often said to young people leaving school.
explain: Try swapping in your meaning. «Pearls are made by oysters and mussels» still makes sense if you say «pearls are made by sea animals with shells». That tells you oyster means the animal.
fact: An oyster is a sea animal with a soft body inside a rough, hinged shell.
fact: Some oysters are eaten as food.
fact: A pearl oyster is a kind of oyster that can make a pearl inside its shell.
fact: «The world is your oyster» means you can go anywhere and do anything you choose.
fact: Oysters filter water to feed, and oyster reefs help clean the sea.
exercise: «Backyard hens are given crushed oyster shell.» In this sentence, what is the oyster? | The pearl | *The hard shell | The soft body | The tail
exercise: «Pearls are made by oysters and mussels.» Which meaning of oyster fits here? | A saying about travel | A kind of fish you can ride | A hard, rough stone | *A sea animal that can make a pearl
exercise: Nadia says «the world is your oyster» means there is a real oyster in the sea. What does it really mean? | A sea animal that is very hungry | There is food in the sea for everyone | Oysters are the best animals in the world | *You can go anywhere and do anything you choose
test: How do oysters feed? | *They filter water | They fly over the waves | They eat grass on the seabed | They chase fish
test: «You're enough to try the patience of an oyster!» What does this saying suggest? | *Someone is very patient | Someone is very noisy | Someone is very hungry | Someone is very fast
exam: In the saying «the world is your oyster», what does oyster mean? | *The world is open to you, to explore and do what you choose | An animal that lives in the sea | A food sold at the market | A shell that holds a pearl
